    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter clearing cursors (i.e. exiting the multicursor session), `]C` `[C` do nothing. This seems like an unnecessary limitation, since the cursor positions may still be useful as \"marks\", even though multicursor is not active.\n\nUse cases:\n\n- allows navigation to the marks; the user can treat the cursors as a generic set of marks, instead of having to manage a parallel set\n    - e.g. `{op}]C` operates on the next mark without cascading.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`]C` `[C` should iterate the `nvim.multicursor.last` extmarks ?",
